  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal Senegal Sea Turtle Stranding Surveys to Assess mortality and nesting.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recipient will conduct quarterly nesting and stranding surveys along Senegal&apos;s north coast from Dakar to St. Louis beginning in January 2016 by foot and vehicle. Additionally nesting and stranding surveys will be conducted south of Dakar for the remaining Senegal coastline 1-2 times during the year. Interviews will be conducted along the survey routes with local people to gather information about nesting and local fisheries interactions with sea turtles. The recipient will also conduct a public education campaign in Senegal to raise awareness of protected status of sea turtles and marine mammals as described in the proposal.</narrative>
  </description>
